WEBVTT

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.470
The sky?

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:57.820
Are we flying?

00:02:03.230 --> 00:02:10.240
Surprised from the sudden collapse of the cliff, Lilan flew across the vast sky with Erin on her back.

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:17.460
Lilan, please.  Head down now.

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.600
Someone's sending a signal.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:36.590
A Crime

00:02:49.270 --> 00:02:49.830
Don't!

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:57.890
Lilan!  Lilan!  Lilan!

00:02:57.890 --> 00:03:00.880
That beast-lord won't move for at least half a tou.

00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:10.710
You're... of the Mist People...

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.040
An Overseer.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:14.090
That's right.

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:18.700
I've been watching you and that beast-lord from afar.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:20.120
"Watching?"

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:24.040
What reason do you have to watch Lilan and I?

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:27.200
You resemble Soyon when she was young.

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:35.110
If all had gone according to the code, Soyon would have been my wife.

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:41.090
I have since become one with the mist, and have been continuing to watch you.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:45.950
In order to save you... Soyon broke our code,

00:03:46.390 --> 00:03:48.800
and used the skills of the Renditioner.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.810
"Skills of the Renditioner?"

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:54.770
Skills which allow humans to control beasts.

00:03:55.870 --> 00:04:02.820
At first, we thought Soyon had told you how to control beast-lords.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.030
Mom never taught me anything like that!

00:04:07.700 --> 00:04:09.560
You're right.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:16.120
What you have been doing at the care center was nothing like the Renditioner skills we Mist People pass down.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.250
"Skills which the Mist People pass down?"

00:04:19.930 --> 00:04:29.340
We are taught with the skills to make sure no one unfolds the Renditioner skills.

00:04:29.340 --> 00:04:34.960
However you've created a whole new skill, all on your own.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:39.060
And that has been our greatest fear.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:44.300
All I wanted to do was communicate with Lilan.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.400
"Crime?"

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:04.210
<i>Since I'm about to commit an unforgivable crime.</i>

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:17.080
Mom said "crime" then, too.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.640
Was she referring to communicating with Touda?

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:24.780
Yes.  And it's the same with communicating with beast-lords.

00:05:26.340 --> 00:05:29.570
Why exactly is it a crime?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.490
I will tell you the reason now.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:42.250
It's a story you must understand, having communicated with and flown upon a beast-lord.

00:05:43.700 --> 00:05:47.030
And what if I don't come to understand?

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:52.010
I may have to kill you and the beast-lord to avoid calamity.

00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.540
Therefore, daughter of Soyon...

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:01.560
hear my thoughts well.

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:11.960
In ancient times, a kingdom known as Ophalon was at its zenith of prosperity upon Ephon Noha.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:16.540
However, attracted by its prosperity, neighboring countries began to invade.

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:23.820
So it came that one of the retainers suggested that the King of Ophalon obtain help from the green-eyed people.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.790
"Green-eyed people?"

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:31.260
They had the skill to manipulate Touda as they wished.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:37.630
The King of Ophalon placed his country's fate upon them.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.920
The war ended with a landslide in Ophalon's favor.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:50.740
Tens of Touda ate through thousands of cavalry, and took the enemy general's life.

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:53.600
However, that was the beginning of the tragedy.

00:06:55.070 --> 00:06:56.700
"Tragedy..."

00:06:56.990 --> 00:07:03.640
Possibly becoming ecstatic over the victory, the King of Ophalon started to invade neighboring countries.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:10.060
Anyone who questioned his judgments faced merciless retribution.

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:15.250
However things were taken too far, and the very same retainer, along with the green-eyed people, created a revolt.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:21.730
The King was exiled from the country and fled with a few men to a treacherous valley of Ephon Noha.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:32.070
Why you...!  First my country, and now you even try to take my life from me?

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:35.530
You cursed Touda!

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:50.170
Are you all right?

00:07:55.510 --> 00:07:57.700
Golden eyes?

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.310
Unbelievable!

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:05.980
A beast I've never seen before is eating a Touda!

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:11.080
It's called a beast-lord, and it feeds on Touda.

00:08:17.960 --> 00:08:19.890
Thanks as always, Luke.

00:08:21.850 --> 00:08:25.960
You're right.  Go home and rest well.

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:30.540
You look as if you're talking with him.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:34.170
They have their words.

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:43.260
We grow up with them, so we naturally become capable of understanding what they want to communicate to us.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:49.230
You're telling me humans and beast-lords can communicate?

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:53.730
Okay, everyone, I brought you gifts.

00:08:54.030 --> 00:08:57.030
I have one for each of you, so no need to rush.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:59.740
Wow, there are so many fruits in here.

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.230
Eat them together.

00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:03.480
Thank you very much, Priestess.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:05.150
Thank you.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:07.690
Would you like one, too?

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.690
You have a very thrifty lifestyle here.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:41.410
People here must wish for a more plentiful life.

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:43.430
"Plentiful life?"

00:09:44.470 --> 00:09:49.570
We use beast-lords to gather fruit in the woods and hunt.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:54.250
We've never felt we lack anything in our life.

00:09:55.420 --> 00:09:59.510
Looks like both people and life here are different from Ophalon.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:06.500
You came from Ophalon Kingdom, which I'm told is beyond the mountains?

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:12.440
Yes.  Ophalon used to be the kingdom I governed.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.350
"Used to be?"

00:10:16.880 --> 00:10:21.700
My kingdom vanished along with my dreams.

00:10:21.990 --> 00:10:23.620
"Along with your dreams..."

00:10:23.620 --> 00:10:25.070
Yes.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:29.780
Ophalon was a country where people from various countries lived together.

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:35.680
I wanted to make a kingdom filled with dreams for the citizens.

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:38.210
"Filled with dreams..."

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:43.430
If possible, wouldn't you want to free your beloved beast-lords from hunting,

00:10:44.930 --> 00:10:48.180
and let them fly through that great sky?

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:14.040
When I sent people to war to seize my ambition, there were people who showed grievance, but I suppressed them by force.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:21.960
"When the wealth, land, and citizens grow and the prosperity increases, they will understand my feelings."

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.870
I thought they would.

00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:31.140
However, no one understood my feelings.

00:11:33.770 --> 00:11:40.190
That dream was trampled by betrayal, and what's left of me now is hatred,

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:45.530
piled together in great amounts like these snowflakes.

00:11:57.830 --> 00:11:59.540
What would it...

00:12:00.590 --> 00:12:03.710
What would it take to free you from the hate?

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:10.220
What would it take to allow your heart to fill with dreams once more?

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:15.700
To give me words of comfort...

00:12:15.700 --> 00:12:17.590
What a kind girl you are.

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:24.190
That's right.  You can do it.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:28.410
You can light the fire of a dream in my heart once again.

00:12:28.410 --> 00:12:32.430
Raise great numbers of that beast.

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.410
Then-

00:12:33.790 --> 00:12:35.870
You mean to start a war using the beast-lords' strength?

00:12:36.790 --> 00:12:45.590
No.  If we show them eating Touda, my enemies will shiver in fear and run away from the kingdom without a fight.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:50.310
When that happens, you should take the throne.

00:12:50.310 --> 00:12:52.140
Me?

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.060
Isn't getting the throne back your dream?

00:12:56.260 --> 00:13:00.850
My dream was to make my citizens happy.

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:10.280
And what I wish for now is the happiness of the people here, who permitted me to stay.

00:13:11.030 --> 00:13:14.530
Our... happiness...

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:20.240
Never.  Even if we are living in this cold weather, we are living peacefully.

00:13:20.250 --> 00:13:23.040
There's no need to seek out more land.

00:13:23.040 --> 00:13:24.210
Elder!

00:13:29.480 --> 00:13:31.470
Everyone, listen to me.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:38.060
We only know of this mountain, covered in snow almost all year round.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:43.150
To get food, we raise beast-lords and go far off where there is no snowfall.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:48.490
We've become exhausted, shiver from the cold, and sleep without even having a dream, freezing beneath the covers.

00:13:48.490 --> 00:13:55.910
But at Ophalon, there is a warm light that's not here, along with dreams never before seen.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:59.330
I want to go there with everyone.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:05.320
A light... and dreams...?

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:06.440
I want to go there.

00:14:06.440 --> 00:14:08.280
I want to go there, too!

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.930
Me too!

00:14:10.930 --> 00:14:15.890
They increased the number of beast-lords to 2,000 over the next 10 years.

00:14:16.950 --> 00:14:18.350
Tomorrow's the day.

00:14:20.030 --> 00:14:23.090
It must be hard to leave your home country.

00:14:24.090 --> 00:14:31.820
If I'm with him, I can chase after the dreams in the new world and fly anywhere.

00:14:31.820 --> 00:14:33.890
I can feel it.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:36.530
Yes, so do I.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:46.000
And so, the moment of truth came.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:58.430
What's that?

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:06.870
This is Ophalon?

00:15:09.400 --> 00:15:10.480
That was the King!

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:14.320
It's the King!  The King's here for his revenge!

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:22.330
It's now time to show them the strength of the beast-lords, to prove to them that it's worthless to fight!

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.410
Everyone!  That's enough!

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:33.000
Don't go after them!

00:16:37.210 --> 00:16:37.990
Wait!

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:45.300
What's going on?

00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:46.420
Something looks wrong.

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:48.080
Luke, go after them.

00:16:49.140 --> 00:17:02.410
<i>A scourge scorches across my hazy eyes. </i>

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:13.440
<i>Uttering a prayer is now only a hope, lost long ago. </i>

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:14.600
What's going on?
<i>Uttering a prayer is now only a hope, lost long ago. </i>

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.570
Why?  Why is this happening?
<i>Uttering a prayer is now only a hope, lost long ago. </i>

00:17:16.570 --> 00:17:18.170
<i>Getting completely soaked, I see a pool of water to the side.
Why?  Why is this happening?</i>

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:22.460
<i>Getting completely soaked, I see a pool of water to the side. </i>

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:24.620
Luke!  Save those children!
<i>Getting completely soaked, I see a pool of water to the side. </i>

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:29.650
<i>Getting completely soaked, I see a pool of water to the side. </i>

00:17:30.270 --> 00:17:31.540
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:34.630
It's all right now.  We'll take you to a safe place.
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:34.860
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:35.710
Luke.
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:41.780
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:41.780 --> 00:17:42.720
Luke!
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.280
<i>The surface is so placid, it gives a reflection of the event. </i>

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:50.480
<i>Wrongness is the sin of not noticing. </i>

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:52.400
Luke...
<i>Wrongness is the sin of not noticing. </i>

00:17:52.400 --> 00:17:53.160
<i>Wrongness is the sin of not noticing. </i>

00:17:54.090 --> 00:18:01.280
<i>Even as the last moment creeps close, </i>

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:04.110
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:04.110 --> 00:18:05.160
Luke!
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:05.660
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:07.040
Luke!
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:09.000
Luke!!
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.120
<i>your soul's voice won't be captured, just like that cloud. </i>

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:16.990
<i>Is this only a momentary thing? </i>

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:23.840
<i>Is this only an illusion? </i>

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:32.980
<i>What stretches on from here is a path for beasts. </i>

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:41.410
<i>Gaze up to the skies. </i>

00:19:01.470 --> 00:19:06.510
<i>A mistake that would cause all humans and beasts to die.</i>

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.680
The beast-lords and Touda went berserk with the blood.

00:19:09.680 --> 00:19:16.360
They could no longer be stopped by the hands of people, and the massacre continued until the end came.

00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:21.490
This is how the world which was prosperous upon Ephon Noha perished.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:26.320
No country has been founded there since, and it is now referred to as the Cursed Land.

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:34.670
The green-eyed people sealed away the skill to control beasts which lead to this catastrophe,

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:41.590
and became nomadic, following a strict code to avoid the recurrence of the event.

00:19:41.590 --> 00:19:43.910
They are the Aowrow.

00:19:45.870 --> 00:19:49.550
Then, what happened to the clan which was controlling the beast-lords?

00:19:49.940 --> 00:19:54.720
She didn't allow herself to return home.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:20:00.900
She flew over Ephon Noha and came to this world.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:04.570
Her name was Je.

00:20:04.570 --> 00:20:09.120
The First Queen of this Holy Kingdom of Ryoza.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:12.540
Daughter of Soyon,

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:21.000
please don't let your beast-lord fly again, and raise her like other beast-lords, abiding by the code.

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:23.610
"Code..."

00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:26.930
I wish you to carry on Soyon's intentions of obeying the code,

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:30.300
which includes purposely killing Touda that have reached mating maturity

00:20:30.300 --> 00:20:33.390
to ensure that their numbers don't increase by human assistance,

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:36.060
and also in believing the Renditioner skills to be a crime.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:39.760
Mom killed the Kiba to abide by the code?

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.070
<i>Mom!</i>

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:54.660
When she used the Renditioner skill, did she really think it was a crime?

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:07.120
Is it really a crime for a beast-lord that's been tamed by humans to fly in the sky?

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:09.470
It can't be.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:14.960
All of this can't possibly happen just because of this.

00:21:16.020 --> 00:21:22.150
Did Mom throw away a future of living with me over this?

00:21:23.060 --> 00:21:27.570
<i>Beasts that are tamed by humans are miserable.</i>

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:32.620
But, Mom was suffering.

00:21:32.620 --> 00:21:39.250
The beasts would have had their freedom in life and death, if everything had been natural.

00:21:39.540 --> 00:21:42.380
I'm sure that's what Mom thought.

00:21:45.640 --> 00:21:47.090
Lilan.

00:21:48.840 --> 00:21:51.970
I promise you.

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:55.330
I won't stop you from flying.

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:10.820
I will never tie you down with codes.

00:22:13.030 --> 00:22:19.700
In the cold snow, Erin contemplated while soaking in Lilan's warmth.

00:22:20.040 --> 00:22:29.130
Erin wanted to find a way for this warm beast-lord to live the way she was intended.

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:06.710
A beast-lord, who should have never become used to humans, flies in the sky with a human on its back.

00:24:07.020 --> 00:24:12.740
It is a wonderful sight that reminds us of the advent of the Founding Queen, Je.

00:24:13.370 --> 00:24:22.340
For this country to return to as Queen Je created, there is something I must do.

00:24:22.340 --> 00:24:25.010
Kemono no Souja Erin.  Fly.

00:24:25.010 --> 00:26:00.030
Fly
